{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The World of Entertainment"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Policing the Paparazzi"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 17}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe situations in spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le17ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Habits in the Past: Used to and Would"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "   You use <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would</span> to talk about past habits which are now finished.  There is an idea that circumstances have changed.  You do not use it to talk about what happened at a past time. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Both <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would</span> talk about past habits which no longer exist, but there are a couple of things to note about the usage of these expressions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "  <ol><li><span class=\"italic\">Would</span>  cannot be used to talk about past states.  You must use <span class=\"italic\">used to</span>.<br/> For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I used to have a dog.<br/> <s>I would have a dog.</s> </span></li>  <li>You use used to to talk about regular, important habitual behavior.  <br/> For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I used to smoke.<br/>  <s>I would smoke.</s></span></li></ol><br/>  Look at the chart for the rules about structuring sentences with <span class=\"italic\">used to</span>.  Notice the change in spelling of <span class=\"italic\">used to</span>.  "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Positive Statement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">He <span class=\\\"strong\\\">used to</span> be part of the local scenery.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Negative Statement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">He <span class=\\\"strong\\\">didn't use</span> to be part of the local scenery. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Did he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">use to</span> be part of the local scenery?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "He would take non-posed shots of celebrities for a frustrated gossip reporter. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Paparazzo would speed around the streets of Rome on a noisy motor scooter snapping away. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "He used to be part of the local scenery."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Secchiaroli discovered that editors who used to want glossy eight by tens, now prefered pictures that took celebrities by surprise."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Secchiaroli would later regret the drastic change in the reputation of the paparazzi. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "He admitted that his attempts to get a \"juicy\" shot used to lead to fistfights and arrests. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Continuous to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress.  <br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Photographers <span class=\"strong\">are hounding</span> celebrities.</span> <br/><br/> You use the Present Perfect to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present. <br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">People <span class=\"strong\">have credited</span> Director  Federico Fellini with coining the word paparazzi.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an  action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it.  Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in writing.  <br/><br/> Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"am/are/is +  being + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Celebrities <span class=\\\"strong\\\">are being hounded</span>.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have/has + been + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Director Federico Fellini <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has been credited</span>  with coining the word paparazzi.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Famous people are being followed. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Celebrities are being hounded. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "This has been happening since the studios stopped protecting them. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Royals, are being chased for photos they would rather not share."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Director Federico Fellini has been credited with coining the word paparazzi. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "This movie character has been based on a real photographer, Tazio Secchiaroli. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Photographers like Secchiaroli have been spying on celebrities, secretly clicking the camera, and then running for their lives ever since."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "celebrity "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a famous or well-known person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Mariah Carey is a celebrity. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when talking about paparazzi. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hound "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to pursue or harass without respite"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Celebrities are being hounded. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Royals "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "connected with or belonging to the king or queen of a country"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Royals, are being chased for photos they would rather not share."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to credit "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to believe or say that somebody is responsible for doing something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Director Federico Fellini has been credited with coining the word paparazzi. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to spy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to collect secret information about another country, organization or person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Photographers like Secchiaroli have been spying on celebrities, secretly clicking the camera, and then running for their lives ever since."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob01aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "paparazzi "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a freelance photographer, especially one who takes candid pictures of celebrities for publication"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He has blamed the paparazzi of today for not setting limits."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "frustrated "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "dissatisfied"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He would take non-posed shots of celebrities for a frustrated gossip reporter. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "eight by ten "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a size meaning eight inches by ten inches"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Secchiaroli discovered that editors who used to want glossy eight by tens, now prefered pictures that took celebrities by surprise. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob01aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to coin "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to invent a new word or phrase that other people then begin to use"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Fellini coined the term paparazzi."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "drastic "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "extremely severe or extensive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Secchiaroli would later regret the drastic change in the reputation of the paparazzi."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob01aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go to the library OR online to look for magazines, websites and newspapers that use paparazzi photos."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out who the current people being photographed are, and note why they are being targeted.      "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think of 3 celebrities who used to be photographed but no longer are."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write up a paragraph about three celebrities being photographed by the paparazzi today and explain why you think this is being done."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your ideas to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find for magazines, sites and newspapers that use paparazzi photos."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about 3 celebrities who are currently being photographed and why using the Present Continuous Passive."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I say what has changed using the Present Perfect tense."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": 