eight by tens, now preferred pictures that took celebrities by surprise.\n<br/><br/>\nPhotographers like Secchiaroli have been spying on celebrities, secretly clicking the camera, and then running for their lives ever since.<br/><br/>Secchiaroli would later regret the drastic change in the reputation of the paparazzi. He admitted that his attempts to get a \"juicy\" shot used to lead to fistfights and arrests. However he has blamed the paparazzi of today for not setting limits. They needed, he felt, to do that.", "id": 2}, {"time": "85000", "image": "engenn9le17ob01re2img03.jpg", "text": "Have famous people been free from blame? No, according to Secchiaroli. He felt that celebrities should face the consequences of their fame. Because there has been massive public interest in their personal lives, they should face the camera.\n<br/><br/>\nHe said that generally, whenever the famous allowed themselves to be photographed, they weren't followed.", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}]}]}